Connect phase predictions to material evidence and kinetic limits (@chemistry-phase-evidence: 0, is #chapter, #hephaestus-core "Investigate-coexistence-phase-amounts-and-nonideal-stability-with-bounded-evidence.lingua#r_000718E1A60501A838E7BA5E84") { r_0069BA0003E1560758AF284230
A thermodynamic calculation needs a material model, a reference convention, conserved amounts and an admissible candidate set. It then predicts equilibrium phase compositions and amounts under specified conditions. Testing that account requires observations capable of distinguishing alternatives: phase identity and composition, temperature/pressure, amount balance, and evidence about whether the observation time and preparation permit equilibration.

A reported cloud point, cooling arrest or diffraction change is evidence with an interpretation. A persistent emulsion can scatter light without establishing equilibrium compositions; a supersaturated clear solution may retain a metastable state; a solid may contain more than one crystal structure or a composition gradient. The appropriate measurement must identify the proposed phases and distinguish a thermodynamic boundary from a kinetic response. Reuse [Review molecular identity through representations transformations and evidence](Review-molecular-identity-through-representations-transformations-and-evidence.lingua#r_0076E2B38375A5256FCEB27DAE) for structural ambiguity and [Explain solution formation through interactions and thermodynamic conditions](../general-chemistry/solutions/Solvation-mixing-and-solubility.lingua#r_4PY91PEG2715V7F8H7MVGP4S95) for rate versus solubility.

In a proposed benign paper study, compare two overall compositions inside one asserted two-phase interval at the same T,p. The bulk equilibrium model predicts unchanged tie-line endpoints but changed amounts. Collecting only a whole-sample average cannot identify both endpoint compositions and their fractions. Independent phase-resolved composition information plus balances provides a stronger test. State calibration, sampling separation, possible evaporation or reaction, uncertainty and rival explanations. This is an experimental design exercise; no experiment or measured dataset is claimed here.

A fitted χ at one temperature cannot by itself predict an entire phase diagram. It may absorb neglected size, interaction or state effects. Compare a parameter fitted to coexistence with independent activity, enthalpy or other applicable data where available, retaining their reference conventions. A single good fit does not establish a microscopic mechanism. If the assumed symmetric model predicts complementary coexistence endpoints while reliable data do not, revise the model instead of forcing the observations into its solver.

Global free-energy preference does not determine the route or time to transformation. Creating an interface costs energy; transport, barriers and imposed constraints can delay or prevent reaching the predicted bulk state. The equilibrium model deliberately omits those contributions. [Separate equilibrium weights from a law of relaxation and sampling](../../physics/core/Separate-equilibrium-weights-from-a-law-of-relaxation-and-sampling.lingua#r_00EE492F15A9D8710F97287B36) demonstrates in a different setting why identical equilibrium weights can coexist with different relaxation laws. Later nucleation, diffusion, surface and colloid formation must supply their own physical laws and evidence.

The NIST reconstruction checks transcription, units, a bounded fit evaluation and a derivative-based inference. It does not independently validate that fit, recover the original measurements, or establish uncertainty absent from the selected source. Preserve the distinction between original model work, published correlation reconstruction and actual empirical testing in the investigation report.

**Work:** formulate a falsifiable equilibrium claim, choose observations that distinguish an incorrect composition/amount account, and identify one result that would require a new phase or nonideal model. Explain which apparent disagreement could instead arise from kinetics, sample identity or measurement. Defend the scope against a critic and revise it without silently changing the original conditions.

**Continue:** [Investigate coexistence phase amounts and nonideal stability with bounded evidence](Investigate-coexistence-phase-amounts-and-nonideal-stability-with-bounded-evidence.lingua#r_000718E1A60501A838E7BA5E84).

